+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 4faa529e55 (crbug 587455884)
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 25-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0010`). V8 15.6 4faa529e55
+(15.6.75.86, 25-11; bugs 590347928 and 587455884; cherry-pick of main 83e9c391a7; M159 twin 548f85215d). Applied as is to
+15.6.75.66 (`isolate.cc` already had a FlyWeb patch; no conflict). Severity not published.
+
+- Fast C API calls jump from optimized JS to C++ without an ExitFrame, so the unwound caller JS frame has a null `sp()`.
+  With a `BackupIncumbentScope` active, `GetIncumbentContextSlow()` compared `sp()` against the scope address: in
+  release builds it read 0 and could pick the wrong incumbent context. The incumbent realm feeds security decisions
+  (e.g. the source of `postMessage`), so this is a cross-context confusion. Now it compares `fp()`, valid on those
+  frames.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`); no bytecode change.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): build and run mjsunit and `cctest/test-api/*` (incumbent, `BackupIncumbentScope`, fast API calls);
+`unittests` `*FastApi*`.
+
 # FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 7ef85e6153 (crbug 587040688)
 
 SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 25-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0009`). V8 15.6 7ef85e6153
diff --git a/patches/v8/src-execution-isolate.cc.patch b/patches/v8/src-execution-isolate.cc.patch
index 668d23c4..223fb803 100644
--- a/patches/v8/src-execution-isolate.cc.patch
+++ b/patches/v8/src-execution-isolate.cc.patch
@@ -1,8 +1,27 @@
 diff --git a/src/execution/isolate.cc b/src/execution/isolate.cc
-index aa4f4fe23e58b14f8e5198afca7b6b091108a445..d3e3fd6f61a8c184e05c4f7cdf575f9e9f5fe9de 100644
+index aa4f4fe23e58b14f8e5198afca7b6b091108a445..236f237d41512ea7c958785cab77bfe8c52de9df 100644
 --- a/src/execution/isolate.cc
 +++ b/src/execution/isolate.cc
-@@ -8739,5 +8739,15 @@ void Isolate::PrintNumberStringCacheStats(const char* comment,
+@@ -4403,13 +4403,16 @@ DirectHandle<NativeContext> Isolate::GetIncumbentContextSlow() {
+   // 1st candidate: most-recently-entered author function's context
+   // if it's newer than the last Context::BackupIncumbentScope entry.
+   //
+-  // NOTE: This code assumes that the stack grows downward.
++  // NOTE: This code assumes that the stack grows downward. Compare against
++  // fp() rather than sp(), because sp() is kNullAddress on reconstructed
++  // Fast C API caller frames whereas fp() is valid and BackupIncumbentScope
++  // always resides outside JS frames.
+   Address top_backup_incumbent =
+       top_backup_incumbent_scope()
+           ? top_backup_incumbent_scope()->JSStackComparableAddressPrivate()
+           : 0;
+   if (!it.done() &&
+-      (!top_backup_incumbent || it.frame()->sp() < top_backup_incumbent)) {
++      (!top_backup_incumbent || it.frame()->fp() < top_backup_incumbent)) {
+     Tagged<Context> context = Cast<Context>(it.frame()->context());
+     // If the topmost_script_having_context is set then it must be correct.
+     if (DEBUG_BOOL && !topmost_script_having_context().is_null()) {
+@@ -8739,5 +8742,15 @@ void Isolate::PrintNumberStringCacheStats(const char* comment,
    PrintF("\n");
  }
  
